<title>GERMANY: Lufthansa sees savings through alliances.</title>
<headline>Lufthansa sees savings through alliances.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>German national airline Deutsche Lufthansa AG said on Wednesday that it had realised 200 million marks in savings in 1996 from its alliances with other airlines and would make further savings this year.</p>
<p>&quot;We expect clearly higher savings in 1997 from alliances,&quot; the group said at a news conference.</p>
<p>It said that its alliance with the Scandinavian Airlines System SAS alone had led to savings of in the three digit millions of marks.</p>
<p>--Clifford Coonan, Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
